WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.967
OUTFRONT tonight, we begin

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.901
with the breaking news.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.303
United Airlines revealing

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.371
that inspectors have found

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:08.041
loose bolts on more plane door plugs.

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.676
As a really sobering right

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.310
just to hear that.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.378
It comes just days

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:12.545
after the terrifying incident

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.446
that you're looking at here

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.215
on that Alaska Airlines flight.

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:15.615
The door

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.851
plug blown out of a Boeing 737

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:18.284
that took off

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:19.519
from Portland, Oregon,

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:22.322
with 177 people on board,

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.924
left that gaping hole in the plane.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:25.692
They were flying right

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.160
in that moment that you're looking at

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.462
at an altitude of 16,000 feet.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.063
A new statement

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:31.364
from United tonight says,

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.066
We have found instances that appear

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:33.500
to relate

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.201
to installation issues in the door

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.103
plug, for example, bolts

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.572
that needed additional tightening.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.306
Now, let's just show you

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:42.509
some images of the door plug itself.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:43.209
That was what was ripped

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.811
from the plane on Friday night.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.980
You can see the size there.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.416
It's about the size of a refrigerator.

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.283
The NTSB

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.151
now saying the plane

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.052
was actually restricted

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.253
from flying long routes

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.721
over the ocean at the time this happened.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.889
Obviously didn't happen over the ocean,

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.190
but it had been restricted

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.792
from those sorts of flights

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.093
because of a warning light

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.394
for pressurization

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.496
had come on three times in recent weeks,

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.731
which had led them to think, well,

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:06.533
then you can't fly it over water

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.967
in case you need to land quickly.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:08.101
Well,

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:08.935
thank goodness for that,

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:09.869
that they were following that

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.371
because they did land quickly

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.039
and everyone it was alive.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.040
Additional maintenance

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.342
was requested, but it was not completed

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.777
before Friday's incident.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.946
Now, Boeing shares plummeted today.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:20.847
Nearly $13

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.182
billion were wiped out

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.650
from Boeing shares today.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.585
I mean, this is hugely significant.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:26.453
Boeing, right.

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:27.754
A stalwart of the Dow Jones

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:28.555
Industrial Average,

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:29.556
a black eye for Boeing,

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.291
does impact all of America.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.992
It is the largest exporter

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.561
for the entire United States.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.029
It is the largest commercial aircraft

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.530
manufacturer in the world.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.665
It is a brand.

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.066
And its airplanes

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.334
stand for American greatness

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:41.968
around the world.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.203
And now you have this on

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.671
top of other disasters,

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.538
you know, of course,

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:46.706
involving those bestselling

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:47.974
Max planes in recent years,

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.542
including two terrible

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:53.179
ones, the fatal crashes in 2018 and 2019.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.914
This now raises major questions

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:55.849
about the company,

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:57.117
its rigor,

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.418
which leads us to this Bloomberg

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.986
headline that we saw today.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.488
China's Boeing alternative

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.823
