00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:22.401
you know, bolts on aircraft.

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:24.337
Almost all of them have wires or pins

00:08:24.337 --> 00:08:27.340
right through them so they don't loosen.

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:28.908
And if that occurred, it

00:08:28.908 --> 00:08:31.711
that plugs should have still been there.

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:32.612
Now, it

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:33.679
doesn't sound like a lot

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:35.014
for little bolts,

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:38.017
but in this case, with that design,

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:39.485
it probably should be okay

00:08:39.485 --> 00:08:41.087
to handle the load in this case.

00:08:41.087 --> 00:08:42.622
But, you know,

00:08:42.622 --> 00:08:44.156
this takes me back to that light.

00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:45.224
We keep talking about

00:08:45.224 --> 00:08:46.425
the pressurization light.

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:46.792
Yeah.

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:49.061
Was that door suddenly leaking?

00:08:49.061 --> 00:08:51.297
Perhaps. Maybe.

00:08:51.364 --> 00:08:53.466
And we just don't and we just don't know.

00:08:53.466 --> 00:08:54.934
And I guess that's the

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:55.801
is the other question

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:57.803
then, is all these other planes out there

00:08:57.803 --> 00:08:58.604
that have the same issue,

00:08:58.604 --> 00:08:59.372
we don't know now

00:08:59.372 --> 00:09:00.273
whether any of them had

00:09:00.273 --> 00:09:02.542
the lights go off before.

00:09:02.542 --> 00:09:04.610
There's a lot more to find out here.

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:05.678
All right. Thank you very much.

00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:06.479
Miles O'Brien.

